 R←∆Test_UC_NuGet_004(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;folder;res;tempDir;msg;rc;stop;ref
⍝ Open project, add a NuGet package with -target=Goo and load it, check where the references are, close, re-open, check again, close.
⍝ The user command used to add the target namespace twice, so the references ended up in #.TEMP.Goo.Goo.
⍝ *** WARNING: want to rename this fn? Keep in mind to rename its folder under "Tests/" as well:
⍝ ***          the test data is located via this function's own name (∆GetTestPath⊃⎕SI).
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 folder←∆GetTestPath⊃⎕SI
 tempDir←∆TEMP_PATH
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 {}FilesAndDirs.MkDir tempDir
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠1⊢folder,'/*'

 ref←∆GetRefToCommTools
 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'ChangeCurrentDir@' 'n'
 stop←0
 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'OpenProject ',tempDir,' -projectSpace=TEMP -batch -ignoreUserExec'
 Assert rc=0

 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'LoadNuGetDependenciesAfterAdding@' 'y'
 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'AddNuGetDependencies Clock ',tempDir,' -target=Goo'
 Assert rc=0
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠#.TEMP.⎕NC'Goo'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~(⊂'UtcNow')∊#.TEMP.Goo.Clock.⎕NL-2
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠#.TEMP.Goo.⎕NC'Goo'

 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'ClearWS@' 'y'
 (rc msg res)←∆UCMD'CloseProject ',tempDir,' -fast'
 Assert rc=0
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Number of projects closed: 1'∊res

 #.TEMP.(⎕EX ⎕NL-⍳9)
 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'OpenProject ',tempDir,' -projectSpace=TEMP -batch -ignoreUserExec'
 Assert rc=0
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Project successfully opened and established in: #.TEMP'⍷∊res
 →T.GoToTidyUp~(⊂'UtcNow')∊#.TEMP.Goo.Clock.⎕NL-2

 (rc msg res)←∆UCMD'CloseProject ',tempDir,' -fast'
 Assert rc=0

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ref.Cleanup
 res←∆LINK'Break' '#.TEMP'
⍝Done
